# 44. DAY 46 KEY TAKEAWAY

> **Anti-forensics consists of techniques intended to hide, alter, destroy, or complicate digital evidence and analysis. Obfuscation and packing make code harder to understand, while techniques such as log manipulation, artifact deletion, timestamp manipulation, and anti-analysis attempt to make investigation more difficult.**

The most important defensive lesson is:

> **Never depend on a single artifact. Preserve evidence and correlate information from endpoints, logs, authentication systems, network devices, DNS, and other available sources.**

### One-line memory formula

```text
OBFUSCATE → HIDE
PACK → TRANSFORM
ENCRYPT → PROTECT CONTENT
DELETE → REMOVE ARTIFACT
TAMPER → ALTER EVIDENCE
ANTI-ANALYSIS → EVADE INVESTIGATION
CORRELATE → FIND THE TRUTH
```